# Legacy C Security Standards

## Mandatory Analysis on Every Change
- **Analyze for security/compliance errors** in all modifications to old codebase.
- Common issues in Angband-derived code: buffer overflows (strcpy, sprintf), integer overflows, null pointer derefs, uninitialized memory, race conditions, insecure file I/O.
- Pay special attention to:
  - src/z-virt.c (virtual memory/string funcs)
  - src/files.c, src/save.c, src/load2.c (file/save handling)
  - src/main-win.c (Windows entry, input)
  - src/util.c, src/z-util.c
  - controller*.c (input mapping)

## Best Practices & Fixes
- Use bounded functions (strncpy, snprintf) or safer alternatives.
- Add bounds checks, validate all inputs/indices.
- Proper error handling, logging (use existing logging.c).
- Thread safety where applicable (existing mutex in logging).
- For Steam production: secure cloud saves, no hardcoded secrets, validate all data.
- Update tests to cover security paths.

## Process
1. Read relevant files before editing.
2. Identify root causes, not just symptoms.
3. Make small, focused, reversible fixes.
4. Add tests for fixed issues.
5. Verify with full build, tests, static analysis if available.

Cross-reference steamband-core.mdc. Fix critical issues immediately. Document in HANDOFF.md.
